{{ 'ka-diary-entry-looks.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- comment -%}
  K&A Client Diaries — Entry Look Spreads. Docs/client-diaries-build-
  spec.md §3 row C, §4 field 6, §5/F1. The core of the entry: one
  full-bleed alternating image/text spread per outfit, looping the
  article's client_diary_looks metafield (list.metaobject_reference
  -> "client_diary_look"). Odd/even alternation via forloop.index,
  same technique already used elsewhere on this theme (spec §9).

  This metaobject type + metafield DEFINITION do not exist yet on
  this store as of this build; see sections/ka-diary-featured.liquid
  header comment for the full data-model + gap writeup (F1/F2). Until
  they're created and at least one Look is added to an entry, this
  section renders nothing for that entry.

  F3 gate: renders nothing unless client_diary_consent is explicitly
  true.

  RESOLVED 2026-08-10: this file (plus 2 sibling entry sections and
  templates/article.diaryentry.json) failed to sync from GitHub to
  staging across several attempts. Root cause confirmed via a direct
  themeFilesUpsert diagnostic call: the schema "name" field exceeded
  Shopify's real 25-character hard limit ("Diary Entry — Look
  Spreads", 26 chars) -- the GitHub sync path rejects this silently,
  the Admin API surfaces it clearly. Same mechanism as the July 2026
  FAQ incident (CLAUDE.md). Fixed by shortening name/preset name.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- liquid
  assign is_consented = false
  if article.metafields.custom.client_diary_consent == true
    assign is_consented = true
  endif
  assign looks = article.metafields.custom.client_diary_looks
-%}

{%- if is_consented and looks.size > 0 -%}
  {%- for look in looks -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign look_index = forloop.index
      assign is_reverse = false
      assign index_parity = forloop.index0 | modulo: 2
      if index_parity == 1
        assign is_reverse = true
      endif
    -%}
    {%- render 'ka-diary-look-spread', look: look, index: look_index, reverse: is_reverse -%}
  {%- endfor -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Look Spreads",
  "tag": "div",
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Loops the entry's custom.client_diary_looks metafield (a repeatable list of \"Client Diary Look\" metaobjects — Shopify Admin → Content → Metaobjects). Add, remove, or reorder looks there; each renders as one full-bleed alternating spread here automatically. Renders nothing unless the entry's consent-to-publish metafield is also set."
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Look Spreads" }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
